    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0691" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>

                <head>265. National Security Action Memorandum No. 100<anchor n="0" xml:id="d265-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-10-05">October 5,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Contingency Planning for Cuba<anchor n="1" xml:id="d265-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>In confirmation of oral instructions conveyed to Assistant Secretary of State
                    Woodward, a plan is desired for the indicated contingency in Cuba.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McGeorge Bundy</hi><anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d265-f3"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d265-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d265-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, RG 330, OASD (C) A Files: FRC 71 A
                    2896, Cuba 381 (Sensitive). Top Secret. Copies were sent to the Secretary of
                    Defense, the Director of Central Intelligence, and Richard Goodwin, as Director
                    of the Cuban Task Force.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f2" n="1" xml:id="d265-f2-content">
                <p>For the nature of the contingency planning required, see <ref target="#d266"
                        >Document 266</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f3" n="2" xml:id="d265-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
